@startuml imaging_service_request_workflow
title Imaging Service Request workflow (excluding MPPS)

autonumber

actor "EHR / EMR\n(Order Placer)" as ehr
participant "RIS\n(DSS / Order Filler)" as ris
participant "Modality Worklist\nManager" as mwl
participant "Modality\n(Acquisition Modality)" as modality
participant "Image archive /\nImage Manager" as archive

group Use case 1: Create an imaging order (RAD-2)
  ehr -> ris: $create-order\n(RAD-2 CreateOrderRequestBundle)
  note right of ris
    Bundle contains:
    - RAD-2 ImagingServiceRequest
      (no Filler Order Number)
    - one or more RequestedProcedure
    - Patient and optional Encounter
    - optional requester and performing Organization
  end note
  ris -> ris: Create and own order/MWL resources\n(Task, Device, ImagingStudy, etc.)
  note over ris
    RIS creates and owns the resulting FHIR resources,
    including the scheduled Task / MWL entry.
  end note
  ris --> ehr: Acknowledgement\n(no MWL resources returned)
end

group Use case 2: Populate and query the modality worklist (RAD-5)
  modality -> mwl: DICOM C-FIND\n(MWL query parameters)
  mwl -> mwl: Transform MWL criteria into\nFHIR queries
  mwl -> ris: FHIR queries\n(resource search)
  note right of ris
    RIS-owned FHIR resources:
    Task (scheduled procedure step)
      -> RequestedProcedure
      -> ImagingServiceRequest
      -> Patient / Encounter
      -> Device (scheduled station)
      -> ImagingStudy (Study Instance UID)
  end note
  ris --> mwl: Matching FHIR resources
  mwl -> mwl: Transform FHIR results into\nDICOM MWL attributes
  mwl --> modality: DICOM C-FIND-RSP\n(MWL entry)
end

group Use case 3: Reconcile acquired images and performed work
  modality -> archive: DICOM study\n(images)
  modality -> ris: Completion / status information\n(DICOM or local integration)
  ris -> ris: Record performed work\n(optional Procedure) and update ImagingStudy
end

group Use case 4: Communicate order status (RAD-3 / RAD-4)
  ris --> ehr: RAD-3 status update\n(RAD3OrderStatusUpdateBundle)
  ris -> archive: Procedure/study reconciliation\n(RAD-4 / RAD-13)
end

note over mwl,ris
  The RIS owns the FHIR resources. The Modality Worklist Manager
  provides the DICOM MWL service and may be grouped with the RIS
  or Image Archive / Image Manager.
  The completion transaction and the mechanism used to update the EHR
  are not specified as a single end-to-end workflow.
end note

@enduml
